            <div xml:id="d842">

                <pb facs="0979" n="867" xml:id="pg867"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.001H61/76: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-08-08T14:00:00+08:00">August 8, 1935—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 8—9:37 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>406. Following from American Consul General at Shanghai.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“August 7, 4 p.m. Referring to the Legation’s telegram of noon today, Vice
                        Consul Terasaki personally and informally requested suggestions as to the
                        best manner to prevent August number of <hi rendition="#italic">Vanity
                            Fair</hi> being circulated in China. I informed him that I had no
                        suggestions to make, that I always disliked for Americans to do anything to
                        offend Japanese susceptibilities but in this case it would be necessary for
                        me to endeavor to protect American interests though I would hear any
                        suggestions he might have to make.”</p>
                </quote>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
